      {
        "id": 236809,
        "name": "Sonvar",
        "username": "Powerhound_2000",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-04-14T12:48:45.291Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"angille\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"28412\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/angille/48/1917_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> angille:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>the health section says to use “The maximum value of your Red status die” — I’ve always interpreted that to mean you would use the larger one and that contributes to your health for the whole character.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’d also agree that you should use the red status die from your personality with the higher size.   Otherwise, as you are commenting, there’s oddness in what happens with the health switching between forms.   The health value is meant to be a static max value not a changing one.   Just like having Form Changer or Modular can alter die size depending upon the form you’re in and that doesn’t change a hero’s max health.</p>",
